HST Office: in a .docx with text boxes, a shape could be imported over the shapes that should
cover it. A filled rounded rectangle then hid the text box drawn on it: only the background and
the banner of a "KIẾN THỨC TRỌNG TÂM" page showed, without its text, tables and pictures.

GraphicZOrderHelper::findZOrder() takes the "ZOrder" of the shape to stack on and sets that
number plus one as the "ZOrder" of the new shape. The setter moves the object to that position of
the draw page, but the getter of SwXShape returns SwTextBoxHelper::getOrdNum(), which leaves out
the text frames of shapes with text boxes. Since the text frames are flagged as text boxes again
(upstream "sw: fix setting mbIsTextBox on shapes' text boxes", in 26.8), every text box below a
shape makes its "ZOrder" one lower than its position, and the next shape is put under it.
findZOrder() now reads the draw page position of the shape (SdrObject::GetOrdNum()); text frames
and pictures already report their position. The extra place it adds over a shape with a text box
counts positions as well, so it stays.

Upstream master only drops that extra place ("sw: DOCX import: fix z-order of a shape over a shape
with a text box"); that does not help when the text boxes are under the shape to stack on.

Test: CppunitTest_sw_ooxmlimport2 testShapeOverShapeAfterTextBox (synthetic .docx kept as base64).
